/* Axes are laid out evenly across their declared range.  An evenly spaced axis is
 * the correct STARTING point and no more: the whole reason the breakpoints are
 * in the calibration is that a tuner moves them to put the resolution where the
 * engine actually spends its time.  A hard-coded axis would put that decision in
 * the firmware, where nobody tunes it. */
